# The direct dependencies of a contributor's checkout, by name: the runtime set plus what the
# tests and the linter need. Versions live in `requirements-dev.txt`, for the reason its
# runtime counterpart gives.
#
# This file used to carry `pytest>=9.1.1,<10`, `httpx2>=2.13.1,<3` and `ruff==0.16.9`, and the
# major caps are gone on purpose rather than by oversight: a range here is the second place a
# version is decided that the lock exists to remove. So nothing stops the next regeneration
# taking `httpx2` 3.x, `pytest` 10.x or a ruff minor with new default rules -- what catches
# that is the suite and the linter running against the regenerated lock, in the same change
# that regenerates it, not a bound written here. A cap that genuinely has to hold belongs in a
# constraints file passed to the compile command, so that it is still one decision and not two.

-r requirements.in

httpx2
pytest
ruff

# Imported directly by `tests/test_compose_topology.py` and `tests/test_dependency_lock.py`,
# so it is asked for here rather than relied on as a transitive of `uvicorn[standard]`: an
# extra that stopped pulling it in would take two test modules with it, which is the shape of
# a version decided nowhere.
pyyaml
